---
import LegalPage from "../components/LegalPage.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL } from "../lib/site";
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy · Up.computer" description="What the Up.computer app and website collect.">
  <LegalPage
    title="Privacy Policy"
    description="What the Up.computer app and this website collect, and what they don’t."
    effectiveDate="November 25, 2026"
  >
    <h2>Who operates Up.computer</h2>
    <p>
      Up.computer is operated by Kirill Gurianov. Privacy and data requests can be sent to{" "}
      <a href="mailto:support@up.computer">support@up.computer</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Your data stays on your computer</h2>
    <p>
      Projects, chats, and settings are stored on your computer. When you ask an agent to work, the
      content it needs goes to the provider you chose, such as Claude Code or Codex, under that
      provider’s own terms. Websites and apps an agent opens through the browser or computer use see
      what it sends them. If you install the free agent, your messages go to OpenCode’s free models
      under OpenCode’s terms. Some of these models may keep data.
    </p>

    <h2>App telemetry</h2>
    <p>
      The app sends usage events to PostHog: app version, operating system, processor architecture,
      provider, model, interaction and access mode, counts, durations, and error categories. During
      setup it also sends which setup steps you reached and whether each agent CLI is installed, its
      version, and whether it is signed in. In the app it sends which sections you open, such as
      Tasks, Agents, or Settings, which buttons you click, and when you first create a task, agent,
      or automation. A button is reported by a fixed name from the app’s code, never by the text on
      screen. Events never include prompts, responses, file contents, file paths, credentials, or the
      names of your chats, tasks, projects, or agents. They are tied to a pseudonymous install ID: a
      SHA-256 hash of a random ID the app creates. To count one person across several installs, the
      app also sends SHA-256 hashes of your UpComputer Connect account and the devices you connect.
      Usage data never includes identifiers from your provider accounts, such as your OpenAI or
      Claude account, and the app never reads them for it. Raw IDs and tokens never leave your
      computer.
    </p>
    <p>
      To turn telemetry off, turn off <strong>Share anonymous usage data</strong> in Settings, under
      About. You can also set <code>UPCOMPUTER_TELEMETRY_ENABLED=false</code> (or{" "}
      <code>T3CODE_TELEMETRY_ENABLED=false</code>) before starting the app, and an organization can
      turn it off with a managed policy. The code is{" "}
      <a href={`${GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL}/tree/main/apps/server/src/telemetry`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">open source</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Connection diagnostics</h2>
    <p>
      When you use UpComputer Connect, the app sends traces of relay connections, with timing and
      errors but not your content, to Axiom so we can fix connection problems. Turning telemetry off
      stops them too, as does <code>OTEL_SDK_DISABLED=true</code>.
    </p>

    <h2>Surveys and feedback</h2>
    <p>
      Answers to in-app surveys, and feedback sent with “Include system info”, are tied to the same
      pseudonymous ID. With telemetry off, or without system info, they are sent under a one-time
      random ID, without IP address or location.
    </p>

    <h2>Website</h2>
    <p>
      This website counts page views, Core Web Vitals, and clicks on download, GitHub, and changelog
      links with PostHog, without cookies, persistent identifiers, or session replay. It respects Do
      Not Track and Global Privacy Control. Hosting logs may include IP address, user agent, time,
      and requested path for security and reliability.
    </p>

    <h2>Retention and your choices</h2>
    <p>
      Local data stays until you delete it. Telemetry is kept only as long as it helps operate and
      improve the app. Data held by providers follows their policies. Send access or deletion
      requests to the contact above.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>Updates will be published on this page with a new effective date.</p>
  </LegalPage>
</Layout>
